%% peer_app_boot.glp --- peer_app/2 under :boot, the app the harness names.
%
% IGLP 4a9ad28, Implementation Notes, "Simulation realisation": "The router
% reports each connection and disconnection to the agents, and reports every
% peer attested with the app the harness names, its developer, name and
% version"; the adjacency relation is total by default, so alice and bob are
% connected from the boot.  IGLP, Definition "Seam Predicates": peer_app
% assigns app(D, N, V), unattested or none.  The REPL's :app names the app a
% :boot reports; alice asks peer_app for bob at her start and tells her person
% the answer.  Section MB, MB7, runs it with an app named and with none.
%
%% The agents' program is the program directory peer_app/ beside this file,
%% which the agents load, this file carrying its boot clause and the persons
%% it names and nothing else (TGLP 6ce148a, modules.tex, "Entry and the
%% absence of a boot module"; IGLP, Implementation Notes, "Boot").

procedure boot.
boot :- agent(ch(_?, _), ch(_?, _))@alice, say(alice, ch(_?, _))@alice, agent(ch(_?, _), ch(_?, _))@bob, say(bob, ch(_?, _))@bob.

%% The person at each agent tells it its name, and reads nothing.
exported procedure say(Constant?, Channel(Stream(Constant), Stream(Constant))?).
say(P, ch(_, [P?])).
